# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAW IMAGE SOURCES
#
# `konten/` holds the original photographs, screenshots and scans — around
# 300 MB of PNG/JFIF. They are INPUT to the asset pipeline, not part of the
# site: `npm run assets` reads them and writes roughly 5 MB of optimised WebP
# into `public/images/`, and THAT is what ships and what git tracks.
#
# Keeping the originals in git would inflate the repository by two orders of
# magnitude for files that are never served and never edited by hand. They stay
# on disk, so the pipeline still runs locally.
#
# If these ever need versioning (a new machine, archival), use Git LFS or object
# storage rather than committing them directly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
konten/

# Intermediate renders produced by the certificate step of the pipeline.
konten/_rendered/

# Generated by the pipeline, never edited by hand.
# NOTE: src/data/asset-dims.generated.ts is deliberately NOT ignored — pages
# import it, so a fresh clone must have it to build. It is small (~70 lines) and
# regenerating it requires the full 300 MB asset pipeline, so it is committed.
scripts/asset-manifest.json

